//
// An arm that answers in the ENUM joins with a sibling arm that answers in one of its
// VARIANTS, and the join is the enum — `match e { Circle{r} => Circle{r: r + 1}, _ => e }`,
// where `_ => e` hands back the very binding the statement assigns.
//
// `formal/types.md` `(C-Var)` licenses `Reference(S) ⤳ Enum(E)` for each variant and licenses
// nothing between two variants, so wherever the siblings have settled on ONE variant, asking
// `convert` for a later arm is the wrong question in BOTH directions it can be asked: another
// variant of the same enum (loft#1117, closed) and the enum itself (loft#1390) each join to
// the enum, which is WIDER than the type the arms had settled on.  The enum arm was asked
// anyway and answered *"expected Circle, got Sh"* — for the `match`, for its `if` twin, and
// whether the enum arrived through a wildcard or a named arm — while the same value returned
// through a function typed as the enum was accepted, which is the workaround the issue records.
//
// The acceptance and the JOIN are one question and now read one predicate
// (`Parser::joins_to_enum`, through `arm_joins_to_enum` at the two acceptance sites and
// `join_arm_into` at the six `match` arm sites).  That matters in the other direction too:
// the `match` join used to keep the FIRST arm's variant however many arms widened it, so a
// variant-typed destination accepted a sibling variant's record and read it at this variant's
// offsets — loft#980's class, refused by the `if` twin throughout.  The refusal cell lives in
// `a-variant-typed-destination-refuses-a-widened-match.loft`, since a firing `@EXPECT_ERROR`
// ends the file.
//
// The CONTROLS pin what must not move: the same variant twice widens nothing, the enum-first
// order still converts its variant arm the ordinary way, and a call arm typed as the enum is
// unaffected.
//
// @falsified-at: 32e36462 — interpreter and native: `test_a_wildcard_arm_answering_the_enum`,
//   `test_a_named_arm_answering_the_enum` and `test_the_if_twin` fail to compile
//   ("expected Circle, got Sh on a match arm" / "on else"); the four controls pass.
//   CHANNEL: the exit channel, measured on --interpret against 32e36462 by
//   `scripts/falsify.sh --bulk`.
//   WITNESS: the control's signature against 32e36462 is `exit 1 -> 0`. That line is what a
//   re-run must reproduce; comparing it is the whole check.
//   HOLDS: assertions, leak, panic, free-refusal, expectations are equal on both trees.
//   Falsify prints only the channels that MOVE and requires HERE to be clean, so each of
//   those is clean on both. The native side was not scored in this sweep.

enum Sh { Circle { r: integer }, Square { s: integer, extra: text } }

fn circle(n: integer) -> Sh { Circle{r: n} }

fn radius(e: Sh) -> integer {
  match e { Circle{r} => r, Square{s} => -s }
}

fn test_a_wildcard_arm_answering_the_enum() {
  e: Sh = Circle{r: 1};
  e = match e { Circle{r} => Circle{r: r + 1}, _ => e };
  assert(radius(e) == 2, "wildcard: got {radius(e)}, want 2");
}

fn test_a_named_arm_answering_the_enum() {
  e: Sh = Square{s: 4, extra: "keep"};
  e = match e { Circle{r} => Circle{r: r + 1}, Square{s} => e };
  assert(radius(e) == -4, "named arm: got {radius(e)}, want -4");
}

fn test_the_if_twin() {
  e: Sh = Circle{r: 1};
  e = if e is Circle { Circle{r: 2} } else { e };
  assert(radius(e) == 2, "if twin: got {radius(e)}, want 2");
}

fn test_the_enum_arm_may_come_first() {
  e: Sh = Square{s: 7, extra: "x"};
  e = match e { Circle{r} => e, _ => Circle{r: 9} };
  assert(radius(e) == 9, "enum first: got {radius(e)}, want 9");
}

fn test_two_variants_still_join_to_the_enum() {
  e: Sh = Circle{r: 1};
  e = match e { Circle{r} => Square{s: r + 5, extra: "w"}, Square{s} => Circle{r: s} };
  assert(radius(e) == -6, "variant x variant: got {radius(e)}, want -6");
}

fn test_the_same_variant_twice_widens_nothing() {
  e: Sh = Circle{r: 3};
  e = match e { Circle{r} => Circle{r: r + 1}, Square{s} => Circle{r: s} };
  assert(radius(e) == 4, "same variant: got {radius(e)}, want 4");
}

fn test_a_call_arm_typed_as_the_enum() {
  e: Sh = Circle{r: 1};
  e = match e { Circle{r} => circle(r + 1), _ => e };
  assert(radius(e) == 2, "call arm: got {radius(e)}, want 2");
}
